{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"28":{"eng-name":"Foods (Kitab Al-At'imah)","ara-name":"كتاب الأطعمة"}},"section_detail":{"28":{"hadithnumber_first":3736,"hadithnumber_last":3854,"arabicnumber_first":3736,"arabicnumber_last":3854}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":3813,"arabicnumber":3813,"text":"Rapporté par Salman al-Farsi : Le Messager d’Allah ﷺ a été interrogé au sujet des sauterelles. Il a répondu : « Elles sont les plus nombreuses des armées d’Allah. Je n’en mange pas, mais je ne les déclare pas interdites. »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":28,"hadith":78},"chapter":{"id":35,"ara-name":"باب فِي أَكْلِ الْجَرَادِ","eng-name":"Regarding eating locusts","isFirstHadith":false}}]}